<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Waldenburg, Saxony</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Waldenburg is a small town on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zwickauer-mulde">Zwickauer Mulde</a> in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. Acquired by the Schönburg family in the 14th century, it became the residence of their Schönburg-Waldenburg line, whose castle was rebuilt as a palace in the 19th century. The town has long been known for its stoneware pottery.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/waldenburg-saxony.jpg" alt="Waldenburg, Saxony" width="320" height="203" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Je-str · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Schloss_Waldenburg_(Sachsen).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
